  "phase_contract": {
    "shared": "Common global threshold; all INSERT operations precede threshold. SWITCH and PROBE can interleave afterward, but actual INSERT/PROBE overlap does not follow from lack of barrier.",
    "staggered": "Different randomized per-operator thresholds permit INSERT and PROBE interleaving. Exact observed overlap duration/count was not independently established from inputs."
  },
  "heat_contract": "Operator probabilities evolve every global operation. Ordinary within-operator partition probabilities remain near-uniform under a bounded slow local-clock process; only train01 has persistent rare_hot. This supplements dynamic cross-operator allocation/large-N testing rather than replacing skewed final_dataset.",
  "limitations": [
    "No raw input or compressed archive contents read/decompressed. Local blob presence/size is not content SHA revalidation.",
    "Publisher validity and capacity figures are metadata evidence, not monitor input replay.",
    "Dev/holdout comparisons use existing shared manifest seed/hash fields only; their input contents, per-case sidecars and algorithm scores were not accessed.",
    "Distinct numeric seeds and exact raw hashes do not prove semantic independence; R71 revisions reuse seeds; R73 small cases share IDs but their read identity file omits seeds, so lineage is conservatively unresolved.",
    "Fixed W/R/penalty100/80/100 and only6 independent train streams limit generalization; exact expected scoring gains are unknown.",
    "Offline probability windows/metadata are not legal online scheduler features."
  ],
